Z||000000||olympic||09-23-2000||03:30 AM||||  Is there a good way to weld cast iron?  arc? mig? tig?  I want to upgrade the front brakes on a car that there is no kit available for.  I can get the proper rotors and calpiers but have to fabricate my own mounting brackets/spindle.  I was wondering if I could weld a custom bracket to the OEM spindle to mount the caliper.  Would this be safe?<P>  Also, does anyone know how to measure rotor offset(sometimes called rotor standoff)?  I know you measure from the mounting surface but where do you measure to?  The closest braking surface, the center of the rotor or the further braking surface?||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||09-23-2000||12:34 PM||||There are a number fo ways to alter the caliper parts. Your problem sounds like the spindle. There is no safe way I know of to put a diferant spindle on. You need to do what we already do to the Fiero fronts, find a diferant rotor setup, or forget it.||||reg||1
